WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.980
Avengers: Endgame​ isn't done giving up
its secrets.

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.800
In the wake of the Marvel flick's home release,
fans are beginning to scour every frame for

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.720
Easter eggs they may have missed in the theater.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.760
In fact, a big one has recently come to light,
involving a villain who just seems to keep

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.340
popping up.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:17.420
You'll remember that in Endgame's second act,
Steve Rogers and Tony Stark are forced to

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:21.449
use their last Pym Particle to travel back
in time to the 1970's in an attempt to secure

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:24.910
the Space Stone, after their attempt to do
so during their trip to the Battle of New

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:25.900
York goes pear-shaped.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.820
"Do you even know what an Idiom is?"

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.880
“Colloquial metaphor.”

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:30.940
“No it isn’t…

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.080
well actually yes, but..."

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.720
The pair infiltrate the S.H.I.E.L.D. facility
where the Infinity Stone is being housed,

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.220
and in the course of the mission, Stark is
thrown for a loop when he runs into his father

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:39.720
Howard.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.100
During their conversation, Howard mentions
Arnim Zola, the HYDRA scientist who was captured

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.890
by the agency that would become S.H.I.E.L.D.
during the events of Captain America: The

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:48.380
First Avenger.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:52.340
Zola was pressed into the service of S.H.I.E.L.D.,
but of course, the nefarious scientist had

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:56.340
a hidden agenda to assist in spreading HYDRA's
influence within the organization.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.740
We subsequently learned in Captain America:
The WInter Soldier that this effort was a

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.600
smashing success, and that S.H.I.E.L.D. had
been infiltrated by HYDRA scum to its very

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:04.400
highest levels.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.970
We also learned that Zola, who had long since
died, had digitized his consciousness, uploading

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:12.970
it into a massive bank of old-school computers
as a way of making sure that he would continue

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:15.040
to have influence over S.H.I.E.L.D.'s inner
workings.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.020
“The new HYDRA group.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.320
A Beautiful parasite, inside SHIELD.”

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:25.740
Zola's Winter Soldier appearance concluded
with him destroying the bunker that held his

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:31.080
digital self in a bid to blow up Cap and Natasha,
but in 1970, he still existed as a fleshy

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:32.000
S.H.I.E.L.D. scientist.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.380
However, there's evidence that his plans to
digitize his code within S.H.I.E.L.D.'s mainframe

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.620
was already in effect by the time Tony has
his impromptu family reunion.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.960
On a desk in Howard's lab sits an old school
computer terminal, and if you look closely,

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:47.540
you can see that Zola's green, low-res visage
graces its monitor.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.960
The folks at Cinesite pointed out this blink-and-you'll-miss-it
cameo in their behind-the-scenes breakdown

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.280
of the Endgame VFX.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:57.640
Not only is it a brilliant callback to one
of the best films of the MCU, it serves as

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.020
a distinct nod to Zola himself.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:03.420
In the comics, Zola has inhabited a robotic
body since the waning days of World War II,

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:07.510
and he keeps multiple spare bodies on hand
in the event that his primary body is damaged

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:08.220
or destroyed.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:11.820
Could this be a way for the filmmakers to
leave the door open for his potential return

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.100
to the MCU at some point?

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:17.240
After all, who's to say he didn't maintain
a secondary site housing a backup copy of

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.620
himself before self-destructing in The Winter
Soldier?

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:23.630
This is a man with a seriously inflated sense
of his own importance, and there's nobody

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:25.720
more loyal to HYDRA and general villainy.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:32.680
“Once securification process is complete,
HYDRA’s new world order will arise!”

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.680
Perhaps this will come into play when Falcon
and the Winter Soldier, the first of the Disney+

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.840
limited series set within the MCU, drops late
next year.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:43.900
Part of the series' focus will be Sam Wilson's
struggle with taking on the mantle of Captain

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:47.340
America, bequeathed to him by Rogers himself
at Endgame's conclusion.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.790
If there's one thing we know about Zola outside
of his unwavering loyalty to HYDRA, it's that

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:55.480
he really hates Captain America, and we doubt
it would matter who's taken up the mantle.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:59.580
This Easter egg is undoubtedly one of a hundred
or so that will become known now that Endgame

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:00.740
has received its home release.

